{-
   A bare `main` with parameters is the program's entry itself (J91).

   # resolver: ownership
   # target: bare

   `-target bare` has no process ABI: the loader enters the entry with whatever it left in the
   argument registers - a boot protocol's magic and info pointer, say - so the entry keeps its
   signature as written and nothing is synthesized in front of it. On a hosted target the same
   `main` is refused (`ownership/Reject.MainParameters`).
-}

fn main(magic: U32, info: Size) -> U32 = if info == 0 then magic else magic + 1
